      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Express $\\frac{18{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}-53x+32}{3{x}^{2}-5x+2}$ in the form $q(x)+\\frac{r(x)}{3{x}^{2}-5x+2},$ where $q(x)$ is the quotient and $r(x)$ is the reminder of the division.$$\n\n| $18{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}-53x+32$ | __ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3{x}^{2}-5x+2$ | __ |  |  | $3{x}^{2}-5x+2$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+15 \\\\  & 3{x}^{2}-5x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,18{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}-53x+32\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{18{x}^{3}-30{x}^{2}+12x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,45{x}^{2}-65x+32 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,\\,45{x}^{2}-75x+30}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,10x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is $6x+15,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $10x+2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{18{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}-53x+32}{3{x}^{2}-5x+2}=6x+15+\\frac{10x+2}{3{x}^{2}-5x+2}.\n$$",
